Q: How can I select all checkboxes from a form using pure JavaScript (without JS frameworks)? A: <p>You can use a Toggle function to select all checkboxes when clicked and unselect them when clicked again. EG:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form id=&quot;myForm&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; id=&quot;selectAll&quot; onclick=&quot;toggleAll(this)&quot;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Select All&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; class=&quot;checkbox-item&quot;&gt; Item 1&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; class=&quot;checkbox-item&quot;&gt; Item 2&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; class=&quot;checkbox-item&quot;&gt; Item 3&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;checkbox&quot; class=&quot;checkbox-item&quot;&gt; Item 4&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
    function toggleAll(source) {
        // Get all checkbox inputs within the form
        var checkboxes = document.querySelectorAll('.checkbox-item');

        // Loop through and set their checked state to match the &quot;Select All&quot; checkbox
        for (var i = 0; i &lt; checkboxes.length; i++) {
            checkboxes[i].checked = source.checked;
        }
    }
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
